msgid "Testing"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"All right, so far so good, but wouldn't it be better with a few tests, just "
"in case?"
msgstr ""

msgid "In the generated build file, you can see 2 test dependencies:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Quarkus supports https://docs.junit.org[JUnit] tests."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Because of this, in the case of Maven, the version of the https://maven."
"apache.org/surefire/maven-surefire-plugin/[Surefire Maven Plugin] must be "
"set, as the default version does not support JUnit:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"We also set the `java.util.logging` system property to make sure tests will "
"use the correct log manager and `maven.home` to ensure that custom "
"configuration\n"
"from `${maven.home}/conf/settings.xml` is applied (if any)."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The generated project contains a simple test.\n"
"Edit the `src/test/java/org/acme/GreetingResourceTest.java` to match the "
"following content:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"By using the `@QuarkusTest` annotation, you instruct JUnit to start the "
"application before the tests."
msgstr ""

msgid "Check the HTTP response status code and content"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"These tests use https://rest-assured.io/[RestAssured], but feel free to use "
"your favorite library."
msgstr ""

msgid "You can run these using Maven:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can also run the test from your IDE directly (be sure you stopped the "
"application first)."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"By default, tests will run on port `8081` so as not to conflict with the "
"running application. We automatically\n"
"configure RestAssured to use this port."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If you want to use a different client you should use the `@TestHTTPResource` "
"annotation to directly inject the URL of\n"
"the tested application into a field on the test class. This field can be of "
"the type `String`, `URL` or `URI`.\n"
"This annotation can also be given a value for the test path.\n"
"For example, if you want to test an endpoint mapped to `/hello`, you would "
"just add the following to your `@QuarkusTest` test:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The test port can be controlled via the `quarkus.http.test-port` config "
"property."
msgstr ""

msgid "Continuous testing"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can also have Quarkus run your tests automatically as you code.\n"
"In the dev mode terminal, press `r`, and then Quarkus re-runs affected tests "
"on every save, giving you instant feedback without leaving your editor.\n"
"See the xref:continuous-testing.adoc[Continuous Testing guide] for more "
"details."
msgstr ""

msgid "Packaging and run the application"
msgstr ""

msgid "The application is packaged using:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"It produces the `quarkus-app` directory in `/target`, which contains the "
"`quarkus-run.jar` file.\n"
"This is a _fast-jar_, not an _über-jar_, the dependencies are copied into "
"subdirectories of `quarkus-app/lib/`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can run the application using: `java -jar target/quarkus-app/quarkus-run."
"jar`."
msgstr ""

